      "card_markdown": "# BOLD5000 Release 2.0 (`BOLD5000`)\n\n## 1. Overview & Experimental Paradigm\n- **Core Contribution**: Bridges classic scene/object neuroimaging and three canonical computer vision benchmarks (**SUN**: `1,000` scene images; **MS-COCO**: `2,000` multi-object interaction images; **ImageNet**: `1,916` object-centric images) using an unconfounded **slow event-related** design (`Chang et al., Scientific Data, 2019`).\n- **Stimulus Design & Timing**: Each image is displayed for `1.0 s` followed by `9.0 s` of fixation (`10.0 s` per trial) while subjects perform a valence rating (`like / neutral / dislike`) to maintain engagement.\n- **Subject Cohort**: `4` subjects (`CSI1–CSI4`); `CSI1–CSI3` completed all `15` functional sessions (`5,254` trials), whereas `CSI4` completed `9` sessions (`~3,108` trials).\n\n## 2. Recording Specifications & Preprocessing\n- **Acquisition Hardware & Resolution**: `3T` Siemens Verio, `2.0 mm` isotropic multiband EPI (`TR = 2.0 s`), accompanied by scene/object localizers defining bilateral `EarlyVis`, `LOC`, `OPA`, `PPA`, and `RSC`.\n- **Release 2.0 Upgrade**: Reprocessed with **fMRIPrep** and **GLMsingle** (`Prince et al., eLife, 2022`), dramatically improving voxel reliability and encoding $R^2$ over the original v1.0 release.\n\n## 3. Canonical Splits, Noise Ceiling & Modeling Pitfalls\n- **Standard Evaluation Split**: Train on the `~4,803` unique single-presentation images; evaluate on the `113` repeated test images (`4` repeats in `CSI1–CSI3`).\n- **Critical Modeling Pitfalls**:\n  1. **Never Mix v1.0 and v2.0 Numbers**: Literature benchmarks prior to 2022 often report v1.0 betas, which have substantially lower noise ceilings—always specify `BOLD5000 v2.0 (GLMsingle)` in protocol headers.\n  2. **Dataset-Source Confounds**: ImageNet images are object-centered while SUN images are panoramic indoor/outdoor scenes; stratify evaluation across `SUN / COCO / ImageNet` subsets to verify models are not merely classifying dataset origin.\n\n## 4. Programmatic Download & Quickstart\n```bash\n# Clone BIDS dataset via OpenNeuro DataLad\ndatalad install https://github.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds001499.git\n```\n\n## 5. Verified Primary References\n- **`chang2019bold5000`**: Chang, N., Pyles, J. A., Marcus, A., Gupta, A., Tarr, M. J., & Aminoff, E. M. (2019). *BOLD5000, a public fMRI dataset while viewing 5000 visual images*. Scientific Data (`10.1038/s41597-019-0052-3`).",
      "resolved_bibtex": "@article{chang2019bold5000,\n  title = {BOLD5000, a public fMRI dataset while viewing 5000 visual images},\n  author = {Nadine Chang and John A. Pyles and Austin Marcus and Abhinav Gupta and Michael J. Tarr and Elissa Aminoff},\n  journal = {Scientific Data},\n  year = {2019},\n  doi = {10.1038/s41597-019-0052-3},\n  eprint = {1809.01281},\n  archivePrefix = {arXiv},\n  url = {https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-019-0052-3},\n}"
