          "Movement-Onset vs. Go-Cue Alignment: Preparatory activity aligns tightly to target/go cues, whereas rotational execution dynamics (`~1.5–2.5 Hz`) lock strictly to physical **movement onset** (`hand speed > threshold`)—misaligning trials by reaction-time jitter smears rotational phase!",
